// №602 (реестр 221.1): `json_test` failed on `JsonObject: порядок вставки
// сохраняется при @iter()/@keys()` — `assert(keys.len() == 3)` — the test
// NAME says "order", but the assert is about LENGTH, and the real value was
// `0`, not a wrong ORDER of 3 correct keys (confirmed by printing the actual
// key list before assuming the name was accurate — the list was EMPTY, not
// merely reordered).
//
// Root: `JsonObject` is `type JsonObject alias IndexMap[str, JsonValue]`
// (std/src/encoding/json.nv). `m.keys()` on a `JsonObject` value always
// resolved to `IndexMap`'s OWN `@keys()` — confirmed in generated C
// (`IndexMap____nova_str__Nova_JsonValue_p_method_keys`), never a
// `JsonObject`-declared facade, regardless of what that facade's body did.
// `IndexMap.@keys()` (registry №506) used to return a lazy `IndexKeysIter`;
// the facade's declared `-> []str` and the actual `IndexKeysIter` value
// crossed at the C level with NO conversion, so `keys.len()` read back `0`
// no matter how many keys were inserted — a type-confused garbage read, not
// an ordering bug. Cross-checked against №505 (`IndexMap.@remove` swap-
// remove breaking order) by READING the code: №505 was ALREADY fixed before
// this branch point (commit bc4857537 — `@remove` now shifts, preserves
// order; `@swap_remove` is the explicit fast path) — irrelevant here anyway,
// since neither failing json_test assertion calls `remove`/`swap_remove` at
// all. One defect (№602), not two.
//
// Fix: `IndexMap[K,V].@keys()` (std/src/collections/index_map/core.nv) now
// returns a materialized `[]K` directly — the only shape whose `.len()`/`[i]`
// go through the compiler's BUILT-IN-type codegen path regardless of how
// `.keys()` got resolved (alias-facade or direct). This fixture prints the
// actual key COUNT and LIST (лесson from №602 itself: names can lie about
// what actually broke — print the values, not a vacuous "ok").
//
// EXPECT_STDOUT len=3 keys=z_first,a_second,m_third

module standalone.n602_json_object_keys_len

import std.encoding.json.{JsonObject, JsonValue}

fn main() {
    mut m = JsonObject.new()
    m.insert("z_first", JsonValue.Num(1.0))
    m.insert("a_second", JsonValue.Num(2.0))
    m.insert("m_third", JsonValue.Num(3.0))

    // Индексный обход (`keys.len()` / `keys[i]`) сохранён НАМЕРЕННО — он и
    // есть предмет пробы: именно эта форма идёт через codegen встроенных
    // типов, на чём №602 и сломался. Сборка строки переведена на
    // StringBuilder (канон perf-conventions): `joined += …` в цикле — O(N²).
    ro keys = m.keys()
    consume sb = StringBuilder.new()
    mut i = 0
    while i < keys.len() {
        if i > 0 { sb.append(",") }
        sb.append(keys[i])
        i += 1
    }
    ro joined = sb.into_str()
    println("len=${keys.len()} keys=${joined}")
}
